{
  "question_id": "q_018_alibaba_compressed_mean",
  "slug": "alibaba-compressed-mean",
  "title": "Compressed Mean",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "company": "Alibaba",
  "premium": false,
  "question": "On Alibaba's wholesale marketplace, order volume is summarized in a compressed frequency table rather than storing millions of individual order rows.\n\nThe table `items_per_order` stores:\n• `item_count`: The number of items purchased in an order.\n• `order_occurrences`: How many orders contained that exact number of items.\n\nWrite a query to calculate the average (arithmetic mean) number of items per order across all orders. Round your result to 1 decimal place.",
  "notes": [
    "The table holds 500 orders with one item, 1000 with two items, 800 with three items and 1000 with four items.",
    "Total items = (1*500) + (2*1000) + (3*800) + (4*1000) = 8900",
    "Total orders = 500 + 1000 + 800 + 1000 = 3300",
    "Mean = 8900 / 3300 = 2.7"
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "items_per_order",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "item_count",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "order_occurrences",
          "data_type": "INT"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sample_data": {
    "items_per_order": [
      {
        "item_count": "1",
        "order_occurrences": "500"
      },
      {
        "item_count": "2",
        "order_occurrences": "1000"
      },
      {
        "item_count": "3",
        "order_occurrences": "800"
      },
      {
        "item_count": "4",
        "order_occurrences": "1000"
      }
    ]
  },
  "sample_output": [
    {
      "mean": 2.7
    }
  ],
  "reference_sql": "SELECT \n  ROUND(SUM(item_count * order_occurrences) / SUM(order_occurrences), 1) AS mean\nFROM items_per_order;",
  "tags": [
    "aggregation",
    "alibaba",
    "easy",
    "ecommerce",
    "math"
  ],
